# Lean/Lake build outputs and byproducts
.lake/
*.exe
*.o
*.olean
*.ilean
*.c
*.json.setup
broken.txt
*.wasm
*.wat
*.elf

# Native linker/debug byproducts (belt-and-braces: normally confined to
# .lake/, but guard against anything emitted at the repo root too)
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.a
*.dll

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# scripts/check_references.py's local, network-fetched cache (docs/
# REFERENCE_INDEX.md, scripts/check_references.py's own module docstring):
# populated by `--refresh`, read by `--offline`. Never committed -- the
# registry (references.json) plus its recorded sha256 pins are the
# reproducible source of truth; this directory is just a local fetch cache.
.cache/

# Scratch/temp files (e.g. NASM.lean's assembleWithNasm tmpPrefix)
.tmp_*
*.tmp
*.bak
*~

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS-generated files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local secrets / environment overrides -- never commit these
.env
.env.*
*.local

# Local MCP server config (personal tooling, not part of the published project)
.mcp.json

# Claude Code agent scratch (this repository is public): `.claude/worktrees/`
# holds ephemeral, per-agent git worktree checkouts that live INSIDE the repo
# directory -- each one is a full second copy of the tracked source tree.
# Being untracked, a nested worktree used to be invisible to git but NOT to a
# gate that walked the raw filesystem (`Path.glob`/`Path.rglob`), which
# re-discovered every already-allowlisted finding at a bogus nested path the
# allowlist (keyed on real paths) could never match -- a false-positive
# generator (scripts/check_gates.py and friends have since been fixed to
# enumerate from `git ls-files` instead, which structurally cannot see an
# untracked directory regardless of this ignore rule, but ignoring `.claude/`
# closes the same gap for anything that still looks at "untracked but not
# ignored" content, e.g. scripts/check_publishable.py's suspicious-untracked-
# file sweep). Also: local Claude Code settings/config generally -- none of
# it is part of the published project, and accidentally committing a nested
# worktree would publish a duplicate copy of this tree.
.claude/
.agents/
BRIEFING.md
ORIGINAL_REQUEST.md
